title ALES99 — Lotus's padded top-and-tail, ALES98 with one honest margin parameter
prompt recur the itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; after ALES98 sent, take the next agent-doable Lotus lap, self-approve, prove GREEN, send as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think ALES98 cuts the dead air flush against the first and last sound — right for a sample library, wrong for a spoken take, where a cut on the first consonant clips the attack. Every recorder and DAW that trims silence also lets a keeper keep a margin — trim the ends, but leave a quarter-second of air. Lindy-first that leader/trailer margin is as old as splicing tape; crux-first it is the decisive generalization of ALES98 — the flush trim is exactly pad=0, and every larger pad keeps that much dead air back, bounded by how much silence each end holds. One parameter turns the sharp trim into the trim a human take wants.
think Correctness is composition against ALES98 twice over. The pad-zero law: top_and_tail_pad(pad=0) equals ALES98's flush top_and_tail byte for byte — run both, compare, so the two tools can never disagree at the boundary they share. The margin law: the result equals the original over [first.start - min(pad, lead_silence), last.end + min(pad, tail_silence)) byte for byte, hand-built by an independent segment scan, so the kept margin is provably exactly min(pad, available) — a pad past the available silence keeps all of it and no more (never inventing a sample), a pad past both ends leaves the clip unchanged, monotone in pad.
think Same segment-find-cut shape as ALES98, tail excess cut first so the leading index stays valid. Kept the two min() clamps as plain if-expressions (pad < available ? pad : available); pad is a plain u32 count with no illegal value, so no new error — PadTailError is just ALES98's TopTailError reused.
obs First witness run GREEN on the first pass — pad-zero grid (8 frame lengths x 4 floors x 3 splits) against ALES98, margin-law grid (8 pads) against the hand-built span, a known pad keeping exactly the named samples, pad-past-both-ends unchanged, monotone in pad, all-silent->empty, no-silent->unchanged, and four named refusals. TAME style bans clean; width-check clean on the new module.
obs No custody gate reached — software only, local; no funds, keys, network, device, or real speaker. It edits only by removing whole excess-silent frames at the two ends through ALES2's cut, never a sample within the content or the kept margin.
loom witness=ales_pad_tail_witness green=1 laws=8 pad_zero_grid=96 margin_grid=8 module_bytes=15k
file lotus/pad_tail.rye ALES99 — top_and_tail_pad() keeping min(pad, available) of the silence at each end and cutting only the excess through ALES2's cut, tail first.
file tools/ales_pad_tail_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs the selftest, asserts the GREEN line.
file active-designing/20260814-234744_fill-ales99-lotus-padded-top-tail.md the self-approved design read naming the pad-zero law, the margin law, and the min(pad, available) clamp.
file lotus/README.md front door — the ALES99 rung and status roster synced.
recommend keep-going — the next Lotus crux builds on the silence family (a min-region-length filter that drops too-short non-silent runs as spurious, a fade-in/out over the kept margin so the ends taper rather than jump, or a normalize-across-takes pass), each its own self-approved round; no custody gate reached.
